=== SURVEY ===
Inspected internal\api\alert_handler.go.
High-level behavior currently present:
- List returns notification logs for backward-compatible /alerts listing.
- MarkRead validates alertID and returns status ok without changing append-only notification data.
- ListRules returns all alert rules from AlertRuleRepo.
- CreateRule decodes typed alert rule fields name, description, enabled, vehicle_id, signal_name, op, value_num, value_text, value_bool, value_min, value_max, severity, and cooldown_min.
- CreateRule currently defaults omitted severity to warning and does not reject legacy contract fields.
- UpdateRule fetches the existing rule, decodes a partial typed rule body, merges typed fields, and persists it.
- DeleteRule deletes a rule by ruleID.
- TestRule currently accepts name, severity, message, and notify_channels; it renders the message against live signals, writes a notification log, broadcasts SSE, and dispatches to selected channels or all enabled channels when none are supplied.

Inspected test coverage for internal\api alert handlers.
There is no internal\api\alert_handler_test.go file.
Search of internal\**\*_test.go found no references to AlertHandler, CreateRule, UpdateRule, TestRule, ListRules, /alerts/test, or alert rule handler behavior.
Existing coverage therefore does not specify typed alert-rule API contract validation, severity normalization/acceptance, legacy field rejection, or /alerts/test payload compatibility.

=== REASONING ===
This prompt is specification-only. It must not add failing tests and must not edit handler/source files.
Prompt 02 must add these alert API contract tests before implementation, then update the implementation until the full targeted test set ends with green tests.
The contract needs to lock the typed alert-rule API before handler changes so deleted legacy fields are not resurrected to satisfy older frontend or backend assumptions.
Tests should exercise HTTP handler behavior through request bodies and status/response assertions rather than only testing repository internals.

=== CHANGES ===
Required Prompt 02 alert API contract test matrix:
1. Create rule rejects legacy fields when any forbidden field is specified in the request body: conditions, msg_template, notify_channels, type, threshold, expression, for_duration_s, and rule_def.
2. Update rule rejects legacy fields when any forbidden field is specified in the request body: conditions, msg_template, notify_channels, type, threshold, expression, for_duration_s, and rule_def.
3. Create rule with omitted severity defaults to warn.
4. Create/update with explicit warning is rejected.
5. Create/update with severity info is accepted.
6. Create/update with severity warn is accepted.
7. Create/update with severity critical is accepted.
8. /alerts/test accepts message.
9. /alerts/test accepts optional target using all_channels.
10. /alerts/test accepts optional target using channel_ids.
11. /alerts/test rejects msg_template.
12. /alerts/test rejects notify_channels.

Additional Prompt 02 notes:
- The forbidden legacy fields must fail even if valid typed fields are also present.
- The create/update tests should distinguish omitted severity from explicit warning so the default-to-warn contract remains allowed while the legacy warning literal is not accepted.
- The /alerts/test target contract should cover both target modes: all_channels and channel_ids.
- The tests must remain focused on the new typed API contract and must not reintroduce deleted legacy fields into models or handlers.

